/-!
# Dimension, Hilbert–Samuel degree, and ideals of definition agree

Let `(R, m)` be a Noetherian local ring and let `d` be a natural number. Three invariants of `R`
that are defined in completely different ways are all equal to `d` at the same time: the Krull
dimension of `R`, that is the supremum of the lengths of chains of primes; the degree `d(R)` of
the Hilbert–Samuel function `χ_R(n) = length_R (R / m ^ (n + 1))`, which is a numerical
polynomial; and the minimal number of generators of an ideal of definition of `R`, that is of an
ideal whose radical is `m`. An ideal of definition realizing the minimum is a *system of
parameters* of `R`, so the third condition says that `R` has a system of parameters with `d`
elements and none shorter.

## Main results

* `IsLocalRing.ringKrullDim_eq_tfae`: the three characterizations above are equivalent.

## Implementation notes

The source's items (1)–(3) appear in that order in the `List.TFAE`. Three points of form.

The source's `dim(R) = d` is `ringKrullDim R = (d : ℕ)`, the spelling Mathlib uses for this
condition on a local ring. No trivial-ring caveat is needed, unlike for the dimension-zero
neighbour [StackProject 00KJ]: `IsLocalRing R` already carries `Nontrivial R`, so
`ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊥`, and it is finite (`instFiniteRingKrullDimOfIsLocalRing`), so exactly one
`d` satisfies the three items.

The invariant `d(R)` of [StackProject 00KA] — the degree of the numerical polynomial
`χ_R(n) = length_R (R / m ^ (n + 1))` — has no definition in this repository or in Mathlib, so
item (2) is written out: `d(R) = d` says that `χ_R` agrees for all `n ≫ 0` with the `ℤ`-linear
combination `∑_{i = 0}^{d} (n choose i) * a i` of binomial coefficients whose top coefficient
`a d` is nonzero. That this is the degree is because `n choose i` is a polynomial of degree `i`
in `n` and these form a basis of the numerical polynomials, so a combination supported in
`i ≤ d` has degree exactly `d` precisely when `a d ≠ 0`; that `χ_R` is a numerical polynomial at
all is [StackProject 00K8], whose conclusion this item matches in shape. The finiteness of each
value is part of the item, as `∃ p : ℕ, Module.length R … = p`, again as in 00K8, and the
coefficients must be allowed to be negative, so the comparison is in `ℤ`. For `d = 1` the item
is equivalent to the form `a * n + b` with `a ≠ 0` used by the sibling [StackProject 00KK]. The
ideal of definition used for `χ` is the maximal ideal, as in Definition 00KA; by
[StackProject 00K9] the degree does not depend on that choice.

Being an ideal of definition (Tag 07DU) is spelled `I.radical = maximalIdeal R`, as in
[StackProject 00K8], and the minimal number of generators of an ideal is Mathlib's
`Submodule.spanFinrank` (as in `ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal` and
`isRegularLocalRing_iff`). The two halves of the source's item (3) — some ideal of definition is
generated by `d` elements, and none is generated by fewer — are together exactly the assertion
that `d` is the least element of the set of the `spanFinrank`s of the ideals of definition of
`R`, which is `IsLeast`. Since `R` is Noetherian every ideal is finitely generated, so
`spanFinrank` is the honest minimum (it is `0` by convention on a non-f.g. submodule) and being
generated by `k` elements, repetitions allowed as in the source's `(x_1, …, x_d)`, is
`spanFinrank ≤ k`.

The proof is organized around the single equality `d(R) = dim R`, from which items (1) and (2)
are two spellings of the same condition, while items (1) and (3) are compared through Krull's
height theorem alone. Both inequalities in `d(R) = dim R` are inductions on a natural number
bound that move between `R` and its quotients, which is why the two halves are stated for every
ring of a fixed universe at once.

For `dim R ≤ d(R)` a longest chain of primes of `R` lies in `V(𝔮)` for its smallest member `𝔮`,
so the dimension is realized on the Noetherian local *domain* `S = R ⧸ 𝔮`, whose Hilbert–Samuel
degree is at most that of `R` by Lemma 00KC applied to `0 → 𝔮 → R → S → 0`. Killing a nonzero
`x ∈ 𝔪_S` — which exists unless `S` is a field — gives `T = S ⧸ xS` with `d(T) < d(S)`, by
Lemma 00KC applied to `0 → S --x--> S → T → 0`, the first map being injective because `S` is a
domain; and `dim S ≤ dim T + 1` by Krull's height theorem
(`ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotSMulTop_succ`). Induction on the bound for `d(R)` closes the
argument.

For `d(R) ≤ dim R` the dimension-zero case is that `𝔪` is nilpotent, so `χ_R` is eventually the
nonzero constant `length_R R`, of degree `0`. In positive dimension an `x ∈ 𝔪` lying in no
minimal prime drops the dimension (`supportDim_quotSMulTop_succ_le_of_notMem_minimalPrimes`),
and the multiplication map `R / 𝔪 ^ (n + 1) → R / 𝔪 ^ (n + 2)` by `x` has cokernel
`R / (𝔪 ^ (n + 2) + xR)`, giving `χ_R(n + 1) ≤ χ_R(n) + χ_{R/xR}(n + 1)`. Summing that bound
expresses `χ_R` as at most a partial sum of `χ_{R/xR}`, which raises the degree by exactly one
because `∑_{j ≤ n} (j choose i) = (n + 1 choose i + 1)`.

Faithfulness. (1) The hypotheses are `IsNoetherianRing R` and `IsLocalRing R` and the parameter
`d`, all used by every item: without Noetherianness the lengths in (2) are infinite, without
locality neither `m` nor an ideal of definition exists, and `d` occurs in all three items. (2)
The base is the source's throughout: the lengths in (2) are lengths of `R`-modules and the
ideals in (3) are ideals of `R`, with no quotient or localization intervening. (3) The source
names no canonical map here; what items (2) and (3) must pin are the Hilbert–Samuel function of
`m`, which is pinned at every value of `n`, and the minimum in (3), which is pinned as a least
element rather than bounded on one side only. (4) The instantiation is not degenerate: for
`R = k[[x, y]]` and `d = 2` all three items hold — item (2) with `a = (1, 2, 1)`, since
`length_R (R / m ^ (n + 1)) = (n + 1)(n + 2) / 2 = 1 + 2 * (n choose 1) + (n choose 2)`, and
item (3) with `I = m = (x, y)` — while a field satisfies the three items only for `d = 0`.

## References

* [StackProject 00KQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KQ)

## Tags

Krull dimension, Hilbert–Samuel function, system of parameters, ideal of definition,
Noetherian local ring
-/

namespace Stacks.HilbertSamuel.DimensionTheorem

open Filter Finset IsLocalRing Polynomial Pointwise
open _root_.Stacks.HilbertFunction.NumericalPoly
universe u

/-! ### The binomial polynomials

The polynomials `binomPoly`/`binomSum` and their degree and evaluation lemmas live in
`Stacks.HilbertFunction.NumericalPoly`; this section records what the dimension theorem needs
beyond them.
-/

private lemma binomSum_degree_le (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) :
    (binomSum r a).degree ≤ (r : WithBot ℕ) := by
  refine (degree_sum_le _ _).trans (Finset.sup_le fun i hi => ?_)
  rcases eq_or_ne (a i) 0 with h | h
  · simp [h]
  · rw [degree_C_mul (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr h), binomPoly_degree]
    exact Nat.cast_le.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (mem_range.mp hi))

/-! ### Trimming and summing binomial combinations -/

private lemma coeff_binomSum_self (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) :
    (binomSum r a).coeff r = (a r : ℚ) * ((r.factorial : ℚ))⁻¹ := by
  rw [binomSum, Finset.sum_range_succ, coeff_add, finsetSum_coeff, coeff_C_mul]
  have h0 : ∀ i ∈ range r, (C (a i : ℚ) * binomPoly i).coeff r = 0 := fun i hi =>
    coeff_eq_zero_of_degree_lt
      (lt_of_le_of_lt
        ((degree_mul_le _ _).trans
          (by
            simpa [binomPoly_degree] using
              add_le_add (degree_C_le (a := (a i : ℚ))) (le_refl (i : WithBot ℕ))))
        (Nat.cast_lt.mpr (mem_range.mp hi)))
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl h0, Finset.sum_const_zero, zero_add, binomPoly, coeff_C_mul]
  have hm : (descPochhammer ℚ r).coeff r = 1 := by
    have h := monic_descPochhammer ℚ r
    rwa [Monic, leadingCoeff, descPochhammer_natDegree] at h
  rw [hm, mul_one]

/-- Padding a binomial combination with zero coefficients does not change it. -/
private lemma binomSum_pad {r m : ℕ} (hrm : r ≤ m) (a : ℕ → ℤ) :
    binomSum r a = binomSum m (fun i => if i ≤ r then a i else 0) := by
  have hsub : range (r + 1) ⊆ range (m + 1) := fun i hi =>
    mem_range.mpr ((mem_range.mp hi).trans_le (by omega))
  calc
    binomSum r a = ∑ i ∈ range (r + 1), C ((((if i ≤ r then a i else 0) : ℤ) : ℚ)) * binomPoly i :=
      by
      rw [binomSum]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_
      simp [Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (mem_range.mp hi)]
    _ = binomSum m (fun i => if i ≤ r then a i else 0) := by
      rw [binomSum]
      refine Finset.sum_subset hsub fun i _ hi => ?_
      have hir : ¬(i ≤ r) := by simpa [Nat.lt_succ_iff] using hi
      simp [hir]

/-- A binomial combination of degree at most `m` can be rewritten as a combination of the first
`m + 1` binomial polynomials. -/
private lemma exists_binomSum_eq :
    ∀ (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) (m : ℕ),
      (binomSum r a).degree ≤ (m : WithBot ℕ) → ∃ c : ℕ → ℤ, binomSum r a = binomSum m c := by
  intro r
  induction r with
  | zero => exact fun a m _ => ⟨_, binomSum_pad (Nat.zero_le m) a⟩
  | succ r ih =>
    intro a m h
    rcases le_or_gt (r + 1) m with hm | hm
    · exact ⟨_, binomSum_pad hm a⟩
    · have hcoeff : (binomSum (r + 1) a).coeff (r + 1) = 0 :=
        coeff_eq_zero_of_degree_lt (lt_of_le_of_lt h (Nat.cast_lt.mpr hm))
      have ha : a (r + 1) = 0 := by
        rw [coeff_binomSum_self] at hcoeff
        exact_mod_cast (mul_eq_zero.mp hcoeff).resolve_right (by positivity)
      have heq : binomSum (r + 1) a = binomSum r a := by
        rw [binomSum, Finset.sum_range_succ, ha]
        simp [binomSum]
      rw [heq]
      exact ih a m (heq ▸ h)

/-- `∑_{j ≤ n} (j choose i) = (n + 1 choose i + 1)`. -/
private lemma sum_range_choose_eq (i : ℕ) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, ∑ j ∈ range (n + 1), j.choose i = (n + 1).choose (i + 1) := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    rw [Finset.sum_range_one]
    rcases i with _ | i
    · simp
    · rw [Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt (by omega), Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt (by omega)]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Finset.sum_range_succ, ih]
    have h := Nat.choose_succ_succ (n + 1) i
    simp only [Nat.succ_eq_add_one] at h ⊢
    omega

/-- The polynomial whose value at `n` is `∑_{j ≤ n} (binomSum r a)(j)`. -/
private noncomputable def binomSumPartial (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) : ℚ[X] :=
  ∑ i ∈ range (r + 1), C (a i : ℚ) * (binomPoly (i + 1) + binomPoly i)

private lemma binomSumPartial_eval (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) (n : ℕ) :
    (binomSumPartial r a).eval (n : ℚ) = ∑ j ∈ range (n + 1), (binomSum r a).eval (j : ℚ) := by
  simp only [binomSumPartial, binomSum, eval_finsetSum, eval_mul, eval_C, eval_add, binomPoly_eval]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [← Finset.mul_sum]
  have : ∑ j ∈ range (n + 1), (j.choose i : ℚ) = ((n + 1).choose (i + 1) : ℚ) := by
    rw [← Nat.cast_sum, sum_range_choose_eq i n]
  rw [this, Nat.choose_succ_succ n i]
  push_cast
  ring

private lemma binomSumPartial_degree_le (r : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℤ) :
    (binomSumPartial r a).degree ≤ ((r + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ) := by
  refine (degree_sum_le _ _).trans (Finset.sup_le fun i hi => ?_)
  have hir : i ≤ r := Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (mem_range.mp hi)
  refine (degree_mul_le _ _).trans ?_
  refine le_trans (add_le_add (degree_C_le (a := (a i : ℚ))) (degree_add_le _ _)) ?_
  rw [zero_add, binomPoly_degree, binomPoly_degree]
  simp only [max_le_iff]
  exact ⟨Nat.cast_le.mpr (by omega), Nat.cast_le.mpr (by omega)⟩

/-! ### Degree comparisons -/

private lemma leadingCoeff_nonneg_of_eventually_nonneg {P : ℚ[X]}
    (h : ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, 0 ≤ P.eval (n : ℚ)) : 0 ≤ P.leadingCoeff := by
  by_contra hneg
  rw [not_le] at hneg
  rcases le_or_gt P.degree 0 with hd | hd
  · rw [Polynomial.eq_C_of_degree_le_zero hd] at h
    rw [Polynomial.eq_C_of_degree_le_zero hd, leadingCoeff_C] at hneg
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := h.exists
    rw [eval_C] at hn
    exact absurd hn (not_le.mpr hneg)
  · have hdn : 0 < (-P).degree := by rwa [degree_neg]
    have hlc : 0 ≤ (-P).leadingCoeff := by
      rw [leadingCoeff_neg]; linarith
    have ht :=
      (Polynomial.tendsto_atTop_of_leadingCoeff_nonneg (-P) hdn hlc).comp
        (tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop (R := ℚ))
    obtain ⟨n, hn1, hn2⟩ := (h.and (ht.eventually_gt_atTop 0)).exists
    rw [Function.comp_apply, eval_neg] at hn2
    linarith

/-- A polynomial that is eventually nonnegative and eventually bounded above by a polynomial of
degree at most `m` has degree at most `m`. -/
private lemma degree_le_of_eventually_le {P G : ℚ[X]} {m : ℕ}
    (hP : ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, 0 ≤ P.eval (n : ℚ))
    (hPG : ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, P.eval (n : ℚ) ≤ G.eval (n : ℚ)) (hG : G.degree ≤ (m : WithBot ℕ)) :
    P.degree ≤ (m : WithBot ℕ) := by
  by_contra hcon
  rw [not_le] at hcon
  have hP0 : P ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, degree_zero] at hcon
    exact absurd hcon (by simp)
  have hGP : (-G).degree < P.degree := by
    rw [degree_neg]; exact lt_of_le_of_lt hG hcon
  have hlc : (P - G).leadingCoeff = P.leadingCoeff := by
    rw [show P - G = -G + P by ring]
    exact leadingCoeff_add_of_degree_lt hGP
  have h1 : (P - G).leadingCoeff ≤ 0 := by
    have hnn : ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, 0 ≤ (-(P - G)).eval (n : ℚ) := by
      filter_upwards [hPG] with n hn
      rw [eval_neg, eval_sub]
      linarith
    have h2 := leadingCoeff_nonneg_of_eventually_nonneg hnn
    rw [leadingCoeff_neg] at h2
    linarith
  rw [hlc] at h1
  exact
    hP0 (leadingCoeff_eq_zero.mp (le_antisymm h1 (leadingCoeff_nonneg_of_eventually_nonneg hP)))

/-! ### Computing polynomials for the Hilbert–Samuel function -/

section Computes

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]

/-- `P` computes the Hilbert–Samuel function of `M`: for all `n ≫ 0` the length of
`M / m ^ (n + 1) M` is finite and equals `P(n)`. -/
private def Computes (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] (P : ℚ[X]) : Prop :=
  ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop,
    ∃ p : ℕ,
      Module.length R (M ⧸ ((maximalIdeal R) ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R M))) = p ∧
        P.eval (n : ℚ) = (p : ℚ)

private lemma Computes.unique {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {P Q : ℚ[X]}
    (hP : Computes R M P) (hQ : Computes R M Q) : P = Q := by
  refine eq_of_eventually_eval_natCast_eq ?_
  filter_upwards [hP, hQ] with n hn hm
  obtain ⟨p, hp₁, hp₂⟩ := hn
  obtain ⟨q, hq₁, hq₂⟩ := hm
  have : p = q := by exact_mod_cast hp₁.symm.trans hq₁
  rw [hp₂, hq₂, this]

/-- The Hilbert–Samuel degree is the degree of any computing polynomial. -/
private lemma hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {P : ℚ[X]}
    (hP : Computes R M P) : Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R M = P.degree := by
  have hex :
    ∃ Q : ℚ[X],
      ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop,
        ∃ p : ℕ,
          Module.length R (M ⧸ ((maximalIdeal R) ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R M))) = p ∧
            Q.eval (n : ℚ) = (p : ℚ) :=
    ⟨P, hP⟩
  rw [Module.hilbertSamuelDegree, Ideal.hilbertSamuelDegree, dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true hex)]
  exact congrArg Polynomial.degree (Computes.unique hex.choose_spec hP)

/-- **Proposition 00K8.** The Hilbert–Samuel function of a finite module over a Noetherian local
ring is computed by a rational polynomial coming from the binomial basis. -/
private lemma exists_computes [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [Module.Finite R M] : ∃ (r : ℕ) (b : ℕ → ℤ), Computes R M (binomSum r b) := by
  obtain ⟨r, _a, b, hab⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_eventually_length_quotient_smul_pow_eq_sum_choose_mul (maximalIdeal R)
      (radical_maximalIdeal R) M
  refine ⟨r, b, hab.mono fun n hn => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq1, hq2⟩ := hn.2
  refine ⟨q, hq1, ?_⟩
  rw [binomSum_eval, ← hq2]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- If the Hilbert–Samuel degree of `M` is at most `m`, it is computed by a combination of the
first `m + 1` binomial polynomials. -/
private lemma exists_computes_binomSum_of_degree_le [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] {m : ℕ}
    (h : Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R M ≤ (m : WithBot ℕ)) :
    ∃ c : ℕ → ℤ, Computes R M (binomSum m c) := by
  obtain ⟨r, b, hb⟩ := exists_computes (R := R) M
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_binomSum_eq r b m (by rwa [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb] at h)
  exact ⟨c, by rwa [← hc]⟩

/-! ### Change of rings -/

/-- Over a quotient ring, the `R`-length and the `R ⧸ J`-length of `(R ⧸ J) ⧸ I (R ⧸ J)` agree,
and the ideal may be replaced by its image. -/
theorem length_quotient_smul_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J I : Ideal R) :
    Module.length R ((R ⧸ J) ⧸ (I • (⊤ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)))) =
      Module.length (R ⧸ J) ((R ⧸ J) ⧸ I.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)) := by
  rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq,
    (Submodule.Quotient.restrictScalarsEquiv R (I.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))).length_eq]
  exact
    Module.length_eq_of_surjective
      (by
        rw [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]; exact Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective)

/-- The image of the maximal ideal in a quotient is the maximal ideal of the quotient. -/
private lemma map_maximalIdeal {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {J : Ideal R} (hJ : J ≠ ⊤)
    [IsLocalRing (R ⧸ J)] : (maximalIdeal R).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) = maximalIdeal (R ⧸ J) := by
  have : IsLocalHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) :=
    IsLocalHom.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  ext x
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  simp [sup_eq_left.mpr (le_maximalIdeal hJ)]

/-- A polynomial computing the Hilbert–Samuel function of `R ⧸ J` over `R ⧸ J` computes it over
`R` as well. -/
private lemma Computes.of_quotient {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {J : Ideal R}
    (hJ : J ≠ ⊤) [IsLocalRing (R ⧸ J)] {P : ℚ[X]} (h : Computes (R ⧸ J) (R ⧸ J) P) :
    Computes R (R ⧸ J) P := by
  filter_upwards [h] with n hn
  obtain ⟨p, hp1, hp2⟩ := hn
  refine ⟨p, ?_, hp2⟩
  rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self] at hp1
  rw [length_quotient_smul_top, Ideal.map_pow, map_maximalIdeal hJ]
  exact hp1

/-! ### The Hilbert–Samuel function of a local ring is unbounded -/

/-- A polynomial computing the Hilbert–Samuel function of a local ring itself is nonzero: the
quotient `R / m ^ (n + 1)` is nontrivial, so its length is at least one. -/
@[ega "0 16.2.1" "special case"]
private lemma Computes.ne_zero_self {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {P : ℚ[X]}
    (h : Computes R R P) : P ≠ 0 := by
  rintro rfl
  obtain ⟨n, p, hp1, hp2⟩ := h.exists
  rw [eval_zero] at hp2
  have hp0 : p = 0 := by exact_mod_cast hp2.symm
  have hne : (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R R)) ≠ ⊤ := by
    rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self]
    intro hc
    exact
      (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top
        (top_le_iff.mp (hc.ge.trans (Ideal.pow_le_self (Nat.succ_ne_zero n))))
  have : Nontrivial (R ⧸ (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R R))) :=
    Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  rw [hp0] at hp1
  exact (not_subsingleton _) (Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mp (by exact_mod_cast hp1))

/-- The Hilbert–Samuel degree of a Noetherian local ring is a natural number, never `-∞`. -/
private lemma exists_nat_hilbertSamuelDegree (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ∃ k : ℕ, Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = (k : WithBot ℕ) := by
  obtain ⟨r, b, hb⟩ := exists_computes (R := R) R
  refine ⟨(binomSum r b).natDegree, ?_⟩
  rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb, degree_eq_natDegree hb.ne_zero_self]

/-- The Krull dimension of a Noetherian local ring is a natural number. -/
private lemma exists_nat_ringKrullDim (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ∃ e : ℕ, ringKrullDim R = (e : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ :=
    WithTop.ne_top_iff_exists.mp
      (Ideal.height_ne_top (I := maximalIdeal R) (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top)
  refine ⟨e, ?_⟩
  rw [← maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim, ← he]
  norm_cast

/-! ### The dimension-zero case -/

/-- In a Noetherian local ring of dimension zero the maximal ideal is nilpotent, so the
Hilbert–Samuel function is eventually the constant `length R ≥ 1`, of degree `0`. -/
private lemma hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_zero_of_krullDimLE_zero {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.KrullDimLE 0 R] :
    Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = 0 := by
  have hart : IsArtinianRing R := isArtinianRing_iff_krullDimLE_zero.mpr ‹_›
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ : IsNilpotent (maximalIdeal R) := by
    have h := IsArtinianRing.isNilpotent_jacobson_bot (R := R)
    rwa [IsLocalRing.jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal ⊥ bot_ne_top] at h
  have hFL : IsFiniteLength R R := (isArtinianRing_iff_isFiniteLength R).mp hart
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c : ℕ, (c : ℕ∞) = Module.length R R :=
    ⟨(Module.length R R).toNat, ENat.natCast_toNat (Module.length_ne_top_iff.mpr hFL)⟩
  have hc0 : c ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0] at hc
    exact (not_subsingleton R) (Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mp (by exact_mod_cast hc.symm))
  have hcomp : Computes R R (C (c : ℚ)) := by
    refine Filter.eventually_atTop.mpr ⟨N, fun n hn => ⟨c, ?_, by simp⟩⟩
    have hbot : maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R R) = ⊥ := by
      rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self]
      exact le_bot_iff.mp ((Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (by omega)).trans hN.le)
    rw [hbot, (Submodule.quotEquivOfEqBot (⊥ : Submodule R R) rfl).length_eq]
    exact hc.symm
  rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hcomp, degree_C (by exact_mod_cast hc0)]

/-- A proper quotient of a local ring is local. -/
private lemma isLocalRing_quotient_of_ne_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {J : Ideal R} (hJ : J ≠ ⊤) : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ J) :=
  haveI := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hJ
  IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- Killing `x` is the same as killing the ideal `x • ⊤`, as far as Krull dimension goes. -/
private lemma ringKrullDim_quotient_smul_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (x : R) :
    ringKrullDim (R ⧸ x • (⊤ : Ideal R)) = ringKrullDim (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) :=
  ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (by
    rw [← Submodule.ideal_span_singleton_smul]
    exact Ideal.smul_top_eq_self _)).toRingEquiv

/-! ### Prime avoidance -/

/-- If `R` is a Noetherian local ring of positive dimension there is an element of the maximal
ideal lying in no minimal prime. -/
private lemma exists_mem_maximalIdeal_notMem_minimalPrimes {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (h : ¬Ring.KrullDimLE 0 R) :
    ∃ x ∈ maximalIdeal R, ∀ p ∈ minimalPrimes R, x ∉ p := by
  classical
  by_contra hcon
  simp only [not_exists, not_and, not_forall, not_not] at hcon
  -- every element of `𝔪` lies in some minimal prime
  have hcover :
    (maximalIdeal R : Set R) ⊆
      ⋃ p ∈ ((minimalPrimes.finite_of_isNoetherianRing R).toFinset : Finset (Ideal R)),
        (p : Set R) := by
    intro y hy
    obtain ⟨p, hp, hyp⟩ := hcon y hy
    exact Set.mem_biUnion (by simpa using hp) hyp
  have hprime :
    ∀ p ∈ (minimalPrimes.finite_of_isNoetherianRing R).toFinset,
      p ≠ ⊥ → p ≠ ⊥ → (id p).IsPrime := by
    intro p hp _ _
    exact (by simpa using hp : p ∈ minimalPrimes R).1.1
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hle⟩ := (Ideal.subset_union_prime (f := id) ⊥ ⊥ hprime).mp hcover
  have hpm : p ∈ minimalPrimes R := by simpa using hp
  have heq : maximalIdeal R = p := le_antisymm hle (le_maximalIdeal hpm.1.1.ne_top)
  have hm : maximalIdeal R ∈ minimalPrimes R := heq ▸ hpm
  refine h (Ring.krullDimLE_zero_iff_forall_minimalPrimes_isMaximal.mpr fun q hq => ?_)
  have : q = maximalIdeal R :=
    le_antisymm (le_maximalIdeal hq.1.1.ne_top)
      (hm.2 ⟨hq.1.1, bot_le⟩ (le_maximalIdeal hq.1.1.ne_top))
  rw [this]
  exact maximalIdeal.isMaximal R

/-! ### The difference inequality -/

/-- If `x B ⊆ A` then `length R/A ≤ length R/B + length R/(A + xR)`: the surjection
`R/A → R/(A + xR)` has kernel the image of `xR`, which is a quotient of `R/B`. -/
theorem length_quotient_le_add {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (x : R) (A B : Ideal R)
    (hAB : ∀ b ∈ B, x * b ∈ A) :
    Module.length R (R ⧸ A) ≤
      Module.length R (R ⧸ B) + Module.length R (R ⧸ (A ⊔ Ideal.span {x})) := by
  have hle :
    (B : Submodule R R) ≤ Submodule.comap (LinearMap.lsmul R R x) (A : Submodule R R) := by
    intro b hb
    simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hAB b hb
  let ψ : (R ⧸ B) →ₗ[R] (R ⧸ A) :=
    Submodule.mapQ (B : Submodule R R) (A : Submodule R R) (LinearMap.lsmul R R x) hle
  have hrange :
    LinearMap.range ψ =
      Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ (A : Submodule R R))
        ((A : Submodule R R) ⊔ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rintro y ⟨z, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (B : Submodule R R) z
      refine Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_right ?_)
      exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨r, mul_comm r x⟩
    · rintro y ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨a, ha, v, hv, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hw
      obtain ⟨cc, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hv
      refine ⟨Submodule.mkQ (B : Submodule R R) cc, ?_⟩
      have h1 :
        ψ (Submodule.mkQ (B : Submodule R R) cc) = Submodule.mkQ (A : Submodule R R) (x * cc) :=
        Submodule.mapQ_apply (B : Submodule R R) (A : Submodule R R) (LinearMap.lsmul R R x) cc
      rw [h1]
      refine (Submodule.Quotient.eq _).mpr ?_
      rw [show x * cc - (a + cc * x) = -a by ring]
      exact neg_mem ha
  have hsplit :
    Module.length R (R ⧸ A) =
      Module.length R (LinearMap.range ψ) + Module.length R ((R ⧸ A) ⧸ LinearMap.range ψ) :=
    Module.length_eq_add_of_exact _ _ Subtype.coe_injective (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)
      (LinearMap.exact_subtype_mkQ _)
  rw [hsplit]
  refine
    add_le_add (Module.length_le_of_surjective ψ.rangeRestrict ψ.surjective_rangeRestrict)
      (le_of_eq ?_)
  rw [hrange]
  exact (Submodule.quotientQuotientEquivQuotient _ _ le_sup_left).length_eq

/-- `R/(A + J)` and `(R/J)/(A (R/J))` have the same length over `R`. -/
theorem length_quotient_sup_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J A : Ideal R) :
    Module.length R ((R ⧸ J) ⧸ (A • (⊤ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J)))) =
      Module.length R (R ⧸ (A ⊔ J)) := by
  have h :
    (A • (⊤ : Submodule R (R ⧸ J))) =
      Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ (J : Submodule R R))
        ((A : Submodule R R) ⊔ (J : Submodule R R)) := by
    rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · intro y hy
      obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective).mp hy
      exact Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_left ha)
    · rintro y ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨a, ha, j, hj, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hw
      have heq : Submodule.mkQ (J : Submodule R R) (a + j) = Ideal.Quotient.mk J a := by
        refine (Submodule.Quotient.eq _).mpr ?_
        have hsub : a + j - a = j := by ring
        rw [hsub]
        exact hj
      rw [heq]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha
  rw [h]
  exact (Submodule.quotientQuotientEquivQuotient _ _ le_sup_right).length_eq

/-! ### Item (2) from item (1) -/

/-- **The Hilbert–Samuel degree is at most the dimension.** Induction on the bound `k`: in positive
dimension, kill an `x ∈ 𝔪` lying in no minimal prime, which drops the dimension, and use that
`χ_R(n + 1) ≤ χ_R(n) + χ_{R/xR}(n + 1)`, so that `χ_R` is bounded by a partial sum of
`χ_{R/xR}`, of degree one more. -/
private lemma hilbertSamuelDegree_le_of_ringKrullDim_le :
    ∀ (k : ℕ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R],
      ringKrullDim R ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ∞) → Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ) := by
  intro k
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    intro R _ _ _ h
    have : Ring.KrullDimLE 0 R := Ring.krullDimLE_iff.mpr (by exact_mod_cast h)
    rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_zero_of_krullDimLE_zero]
    simp
  | succ k ih =>
    intro R _ _ _ h
    by_cases h0 : Ring.KrullDimLE 0 R
    · rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_zero_of_krullDimLE_zero]
      exact le_trans (le_of_eq rfl) (by exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le (k + 1))
    obtain ⟨x, hxm, hxnot⟩ := exists_mem_maximalIdeal_notMem_minimalPrimes h0
    have hJtop : (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R) ≠ ⊤ :=
      ne_top_of_le_ne_top (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top
        (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hxm))
    have hlocT := isLocalRing_quotient_of_ne_top hJtop
    -- `dim R/xR ≤ k`
    have hdrop : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) + 1 ≤ ringKrullDim R := by
      have hann : ∀ p ∈ (Module.annihilator R R).minimalPrimes, x ∉ p := by
        rw [Module.annihilator_eq_bot.mpr (inferInstance : FaithfulSMul R R)]
        exact hxnot
      have h1 := Module.supportDim_quotSMulTop_succ_le_of_notMem_minimalPrimes (M := R) hann
      have h2 : Module.supportDim R (QuotSMulTop x R) = ringKrullDim (R ⧸ x • (⊤ : Ideal R)) :=
        Module.supportDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim (x • (⊤ : Ideal R))
      rw [Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim, h2, ringKrullDim_quotient_smul_top] at h1
      exact h1
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := exists_nat_ringKrullDim (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R))
    have hjk : j ≤ k := by
      rw [hj] at hdrop
      have h2 : ((j + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ((k + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
        push_cast
        exact hdrop.trans h
      have : j + 1 ≤ k + 1 := by exact_mod_cast h2
      omega
    have hT :
      Module.hilbertSamuelDegree (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R))
          (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) ≤
        (k : WithBot ℕ) :=
      le_trans
        (ih _
          (by
            rw [hj]; exact_mod_cast hjk))
        (le_refl _)
    -- transfer to a binomial combination indexed by `k`
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_computes_binomSum_of_degree_le (R := R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R))
      (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) hT
    have hQ : Computes R (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) (binomSum k c) :=
      hc.of_quotient hJtop
    obtain ⟨r1, b1, hb1⟩ := exists_computes (R := R) R
    -- the pointwise bound `χ_R(n + 1) ≤ χ_R(n) + χ_T(n + 1)`
    have hpoint :
      ∀ n : ℕ,
        Module.length R (R ⧸ (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1 + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R R))) ≤
          Module.length R (R ⧸ (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R R))) +
            Module.length R
              ((R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R)) ⧸
                (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1 + 1) •
                  (⊤ : Submodule R (R ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal R))))) := by
      intro n
      rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self, Ideal.smul_top_eq_self, length_quotient_sup_eq]
      refine length_quotient_le_add x (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1 + 1)) (maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) ?_
      intro b hb
      have hmem := Ideal.mul_mem_mul hxm hb
      have hpow : maximalIdeal R * maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1) = maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1 + 1) := by
        ring
      rwa [hpow] at hmem
    obtain ⟨N1, hN1⟩ := Filter.eventually_atTop.mp hb1
    obtain ⟨N2, hN2⟩ := Filter.eventually_atTop.mp hQ
    obtain ⟨N, hNa, hNb⟩ : ∃ N : ℕ, N1 ≤ N ∧ N2 ≤ N :=
      ⟨max N1 N2, le_max_left _ _, le_max_right _ _⟩
    -- one step of the recursion, at the level of the computing polynomials
    have hrec :
      ∀ n : ℕ,
        N ≤ n →
          (binomSum r1 b1).eval ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℚ) ≤
            (binomSum r1 b1).eval ((n : ℕ) : ℚ) + (binomSum k c).eval ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℚ) := by
      intro n hn
      obtain ⟨p, hp1, hp2⟩ := hN1 n (le_trans hNa hn)
      obtain ⟨p', hp1', hp2'⟩ := hN1 (n + 1) (by omega)
      obtain ⟨q', hq1', hq2'⟩ := hN2 (n + 1) (by omega)
      have hle := hpoint n
      rw [hp1', hp1, hq1'] at hle
      have hnat : p' ≤ p + q' := by exact_mod_cast hle
      rw [hp2, hp2', hq2']
      exact_mod_cast hnat
    -- telescoping
    have htel :
      ∀ i : ℕ,
        (binomSum r1 b1).eval ((N + i : ℕ) : ℚ) ≤
          (binomSum r1 b1).eval ((N : ℕ) : ℚ) +
            ∑ j ∈ range i, (binomSum k c).eval ((N + 1 + j : ℕ) : ℚ) := by
      intro i
      induction i with
      | zero => simp
      | succ i ihi =>
        have e1 : N + (i + 1) = N + i + 1 := by omega
        have e2 : N + 1 + i = N + i + 1 := by omega
        rw [e1, Finset.sum_range_succ, e2]
        have h1 := hrec (N + i) (by omega)
        linarith [h1, ihi]
    -- assemble the bounding polynomial
    rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb1]
    refine
      degree_le_of_eventually_le (G :=
        C
            ((binomSum r1 b1).eval ((N : ℕ) : ℚ) -
              ∑ j ∈ range (N + 1), (binomSum k c).eval ((j : ℕ) : ℚ)) +
          binomSumPartial k c)
        ?_ ?_ ?_
    · filter_upwards [hb1] with n hn
      obtain ⟨p, -, hp2⟩ := hn
      rw [hp2]
      positivity
    · refine Filter.eventually_atTop.mpr ⟨N, fun n hn => ?_⟩
      have hi : n = N + (n - N) := by omega
      have h3 := htel (n - N)
      rw [← hi] at h3
      rw [eval_add, eval_C, binomSumPartial_eval]
      have hsplit2 :
        ∑ j ∈ range (n + 1), (binomSum k c).eval ((j : ℕ) : ℚ) =
          (∑ j ∈ range (N + 1), (binomSum k c).eval ((j : ℕ) : ℚ)) +
            ∑ j ∈ range (n - N), (binomSum k c).eval (((N + 1 + j : ℕ)) : ℚ) := by
        have hn1 : n + 1 = (N + 1) + (n - N) := by omega
        rw [hn1, Finset.sum_range_add]
      rw [hsplit2]
      linarith [h3]
    · refine le_trans (degree_add_le _ _) ?_
      simp only [max_le_iff]
      exact
        ⟨le_trans degree_C_le (by exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le (k + 1)),
          binomSumPartial_degree_le k c⟩

/-! ### Items (1) and (3) -/

section Three

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]

/-- The height of an ideal depends only on its radical. -/
private lemma radical_height {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) :
    I.radical.height = I.height := by
  rw [Ideal.height_eq_inf_minimalPrimes, Ideal.height_eq_inf_minimalPrimes,
    Ideal.radical_minimalPrimes]

/-- **An ideal of definition has at least `dim R` generators.** -/
private lemma ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_of_radical_eq_maximalIdeal {I : Ideal R}
    (h : I.radical = maximalIdeal R) : ringKrullDim R ≤ ((I.spanFinrank : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hne : I ≠ ⊤ := fun e =>
    (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top (by rw [← h, e, Ideal.radical_top])
  calc
    ringKrullDim R = ((maximalIdeal R).height : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
      maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim.symm
    _ = ((I.height : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [← h, radical_height]
    _ ≤ ((I.spanFinrank : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by exact_mod_cast Ideal.height_le_spanFinrank I hne

/-- **Item (3) from item (1).** If `dim R = e` then `e` is the least number of generators of an
ideal of definition of `R`. -/
private lemma isLeast_spanFinrank {e : ℕ} (he : ringKrullDim R = (e : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    IsLeast {n : ℕ | ∃ I : Ideal R, I.radical = maximalIdeal R ∧ I.spanFinrank = n} e := by
  classical
  have hlow :
    ∀ n ∈ {n : ℕ | ∃ I : Ideal R, I.radical = maximalIdeal R ∧ I.spanFinrank = n}, e ≤ n := by
    rintro n ⟨I, hI, rfl⟩
    have h2 : ((e : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ((I.spanFinrank : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      rw [show (((e : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞)) = ringKrullDim R by
          rw [he]; norm_cast]
      exact ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_of_radical_eq_maximalIdeal hI
    exact_mod_cast h2
  refine ⟨?_, hlow⟩
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hcard⟩ := Ideal.exists_finset_card_eq_height_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal R)
  have hrad : (Ideal.span (s : Set R)).radical = maximalIdeal R := by
    rw [Ideal.radical_eq_sInf]
    exact le_antisymm (sInf_le ⟨hs.1.2, (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).isPrime⟩)
      (le_sInf fun J hJ => hs.2 ⟨hJ.2, hJ.1⟩ (le_maximalIdeal hJ.2.ne_top))
  have hcard_e : s.card = e := by
    have h1 : ((s.card : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim R := by
      rw [hcard, maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim]
    rw [he] at h1
    exact_mod_cast h1
  have hle : (Ideal.span (s : Set R)).spanFinrank ≤ e := by
    refine (Submodule.spanFinrank_span_le_ncard_of_finite s.finite_toSet).trans ?_
    rw [Set.ncard_coe_finset, hcard_e]
  exact ⟨Ideal.span (s : Set R), hrad, le_antisymm hle (hlow _ ⟨_, hrad, rfl⟩)⟩

end Three

/-! ### The dimension is realized on a quotient by a prime -/

/-- The Krull dimension of `R` is at most that of `R ⧸ 𝔮` for the smallest prime `𝔮` of some
longest chain of primes: that chain lies entirely in `V(𝔮)`. -/
private lemma exists_prime_ringKrullDim_le_quotient (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ∃ q : Ideal R, q.IsPrime ∧ ringKrullDim R ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ q) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_nat_ringKrullDim R
  have hge : ((e : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ Order.krullDim (PrimeSpectrum R) := he.ge
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := Order.le_krullDim_iff.mp hge
  refine ⟨(l.head).asIdeal, (l.head).isPrime, ?_⟩
  rw [he, ringKrullDim_quotient]
  refine Order.le_krullDim_iff.mpr
    ⟨{ length := l.length
       toFun := fun i =>
         ⟨l.toFun i, by
           have h : (l.head).asIdeal ≤ (l.toFun i).asIdeal := l.monotone (Fin.zero_le i)
           rw [PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus]
           exact SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr h⟩
       step := fun i => l.step i }, hl⟩

/-! ### Item (1) from item (2) -/

/-- **The dimension is at most the Hilbert–Samuel degree.** Induction on the bound `k`: if
`dim R > 0`, pass to `S = R ⧸ 𝔮` realizing the dimension, which is a domain, kill a nonzero
`x ∈ 𝔪_S` to get `T`, and use that `d(T) < d(S) ≤ d(R)` while `dim S ≤ dim T + 1`. -/
@[ega "0 16.2.3.2" "special case"]
private lemma ringKrullDim_le_of_hilbertSamuelDegree_le :
    ∀ (k : ℕ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R],
      Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ) → ringKrullDim R ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  intro k
  induction k using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | _ k ih =>
    intro R _ _ _ hR
    -- If `dim R = 0` there is nothing to do.
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_nat_ringKrullDim R
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos e with rfl | hepos
    · rw [he]; exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le k
    -- Pass to `S = R ⧸ 𝔮`, a Noetherian local domain of the same dimension.
    obtain ⟨q, hq, hqle⟩ := exists_prime_ringKrullDim_le_quotient R
    have hqtop : q ≠ ⊤ := hq.ne_top
    have hlocS := isLocalRing_quotient_of_ne_top hqtop
    have : IsDomain (R ⧸ q) := Ideal.Quotient.isDomain q
    -- `d(S) ≤ d(R)`, by Lemma 00KC applied to `0 → 𝔮 → R → S → 0`.
    have hSR : Module.hilbertSamuelDegree (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ) := by
      obtain ⟨r, b, hb⟩ := exists_computes (R := R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q)
      have hRb : Computes R (R ⧸ q) (binomSum r b) := hb.of_quotient hqtop
      have h00KC :=
        (Ideal.max_degree_eq_degree_of_exact (maximalIdeal R) (radical_maximalIdeal R) (f :=
            (q : Submodule R R).subtype) (g := (q : Submodule R R).mkQ)
            (LinearMap.exact_subtype_mkQ _) Subtype.coe_injective (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)).2
      have h1 : (binomSum r b).degree = (maximalIdeal R).hilbertSamuelDegree (R ⧸ q) :=
        (hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hRb).symm
      rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb, h1]
      exact le_trans (le_trans (le_max_right _ _) h00KC.le) hR
    -- `S` is not a field, so its maximal ideal has a nonzero element.
    have hdimS : ((e : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ q) := by
      rw [← he]; exact hqle
    have hmne : maximalIdeal (R ⧸ q) ≠ ⊥ := by
      intro hbot
      rw [ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_isField (isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.mpr hbot)] at hdimS
      have : (e : ℕ) ≤ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hdimS
      omega
    obtain ⟨x, hxm, hx0⟩ := (Submodule.ne_bot_iff _).mp hmne
    have hspan_le : (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)) ≤ maximalIdeal (R ⧸ q) :=
      Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hxm)
    have hJtop : (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)) ≠ ⊤ :=
      ne_top_of_le_ne_top (maximalIdeal.isMaximal (R ⧸ q)).ne_top hspan_le
    have hlocT := isLocalRing_quotient_of_ne_top hJtop
    -- `d(T) < d(S)`, by Lemma 00KC applied to `0 → S --x--> S → T → 0`.
    have hTS :
      Module.hilbertSamuelDegree ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)))
          ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q))) <
        Module.hilbertSamuelDegree (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) := by
      obtain ⟨r1, b1, hb1⟩ := exists_computes (R := R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q)
      obtain ⟨r2, b2, hb2⟩ :=
        exists_computes (R := (R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)))
          ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)))
      have hb2' : Computes (R ⧸ q) ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q))) (binomSum r2 b2) :=
        hb2.of_quotient hJtop
      have hInj : Function.Injective (LinearMap.lsmul (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) x) := by
        intro a b hab
        exact mul_left_cancel₀ hx0 (by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hab)
      have hrange :
        LinearMap.range (LinearMap.lsmul (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) x) =
          (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)) := by
        ext y
        constructor
        · rintro ⟨z, rfl⟩
          exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨z, by simp [smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]⟩
        · intro hy
          obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hy
          exact ⟨c, by simp [smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]⟩
      have hExact :
        Function.Exact (LinearMap.lsmul (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) x)
          ((Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)) : Submodule (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q)).mkQ := by
        rw [LinearMap.exact_iff, Submodule.ker_mkQ, hrange]
      have hfin : ¬IsFiniteLength (R ⧸ q) (R ⧸ q) := by
        intro hFL
        have hart : IsArtinianRing (R ⧸ q) := (isArtinianRing_iff_isFiniteLength _).mpr hFL
        have : Ring.KrullDimLE 0 (R ⧸ q) := isArtinianRing_iff_krullDimLE_zero.mp hart
        have hbot : (⊥ : Ideal (R ⧸ q)) = maximalIdeal (R ⧸ q) :=
          Ring.KrullDimLE.eq_maximalIdeal_of_isPrime ⊥
        exact hx0 (by simpa [← hbot] using hxm)
      have hmain :=
        (Ideal.max_degree_eq_degree_of_exact (maximalIdeal (R ⧸ q)) (radical_maximalIdeal (R ⧸ q))
              hExact hInj (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)).1
          (binomSum r1 b1) (binomSum r1 b1) (binomSum r2 b2) hb1 hb1 hb2'
      have hlt := hmain.1 hfin
      have hsimp : binomSum r1 b1 - binomSum r2 b2 - binomSum r1 b1 = -(binomSum r2 b2) := by ring
      rw [hsimp, degree_neg] at hlt
      rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb2, hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hb1]
      exact hlt
    -- The induction.
    obtain ⟨jT, hjT⟩ := exists_nat_hilbertSamuelDegree ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q)))
    obtain ⟨jS, hjS⟩ := exists_nat_hilbertSamuelDegree (R ⧸ q)
    rw [hjT, hjS] at hTS
    have hjTS : jT < jS := by exact_mod_cast hTS
    have hjSk : jS ≤ k := by
      rw [hjS] at hSR; exact_mod_cast hSR
    have hdimT :
      ringKrullDim ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q))) ≤ ((jT : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
      ih jT (lt_of_lt_of_le hjTS hjSk) _ (le_of_eq hjT)
    have hstep :
      ringKrullDim (R ⧸ q) ≤ ringKrullDim ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q))) + 1 := by
      refine le_trans (ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotSMulTop_succ hxm) ?_
      rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_smul_top]
    have hfinal : ((jT : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      exact_mod_cast lt_of_lt_of_le hjTS hjSk
    calc
      ringKrullDim R ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ q) := hqle
      _ ≤ ringKrullDim ((R ⧸ q) ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal (R ⧸ q))) + 1 := hstep
      _ ≤ ((jT : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 := by gcongr
      _ ≤ (k : WithBot ℕ∞) := hfinal

/-! ### The dimension theorem -/

/-- **The Hilbert–Samuel degree of a Noetherian local ring is its Krull dimension.** -/
private lemma hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_ringKrullDim (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {e : ℕ} (he : ringKrullDim R = (e : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = (e : WithBot ℕ) := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := exists_nat_hilbertSamuelDegree R
  have h1 : ringKrullDim R ≤ (j : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ringKrullDim_le_of_hilbertSamuelDegree_le j R (le_of_eq hj)
  have h2 : Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R ≤ (e : WithBot ℕ) :=
    hilbertSamuelDegree_le_of_ringKrullDim_le e R (le_of_eq he)
  rw [he] at h1
  have hej : e ≤ j := by exact_mod_cast h1
  rw [hj] at h2
  have hje : j ≤ e := by exact_mod_cast h2
  rw [hj, le_antisymm hje hej]

/-- Item (2) of the proposition — that the Hilbert–Samuel function is eventually the `ℤ`-linear
combination `∑_{i ≤ d} (n choose i) a i` of binomial coefficients with `a d ≠ 0` — says exactly
that the Hilbert–Samuel degree of `R` is `d`. -/
private lemma item_two_iff {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (d : ℕ) :
    (∃ a : ℕ → ℤ,
        a d ≠ 0 ∧
          ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop,
            ∃ p : ℕ,
              Module.length R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) = p ∧
                (p : ℤ) = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (d + 1), (n.choose i : ℤ) * a i) ↔
      Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = (d : WithBot ℕ) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, ha0, ha⟩
    have hcomp : Computes R R (binomSum d a) := by
      filter_upwards [ha] with n hn
      obtain ⟨p, hp1, hp2⟩ := hn
      refine ⟨p, by rwa [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self], ?_⟩
      rw [binomSum_eval, ← hp2]
      push_cast
      ring
    rw [hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hcomp, binomSum_degree d a ha0]
  · intro hd
    obtain ⟨c, hcomp⟩ := exists_computes_binomSum_of_degree_le R hd.le
    have hdegc : (binomSum d c).degree = (d : WithBot ℕ) := by
      rw [← hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_degree hcomp, hd]
    have hne : binomSum d c ≠ 0 := fun h0 => by
      rw [h0, degree_zero] at hdegc
      exact absurd hdegc (by simp)
    have hcd : c d ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      have hnd : (binomSum d c).natDegree = d := natDegree_eq_of_degree_eq_some hdegc
      have hlc : (binomSum d c).leadingCoeff = 0 := by
        rw [leadingCoeff, hnd, coeff_binomSum_self, h0]
        simp
      exact hne (leadingCoeff_eq_zero.mp hlc)
    refine ⟨c, hcd, ?_⟩
    filter_upwards [hcomp] with n hn
    obtain ⟨p, hp1, hp2⟩ := hn
    rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_self] at hp1
    refine ⟨p, hp1, ?_⟩
    rw [binomSum_eval] at hp2
    exact_mod_cast hp2.symm

/-- The three characterizations of `d` for a Noetherian local ring `R` — `dim R = d`, the
Hilbert–Samuel function of `R` eventually a binomial combination of degree `d`, and `d` the least
number of generators of an ideal of definition — are equivalent. -/
public theorem solution {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (d : ℕ) :
    List.TFAE
      [ringKrullDim R = d,
        ∃ a : ℕ → ℤ,
          a d ≠ 0 ∧
            ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop,
              ∃ p : ℕ,
                Module.length R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) = p ∧
                  (p : ℤ) = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (d + 1), (n.choose i : ℤ) * a i,
        IsLeast {n : ℕ | ∃ I : Ideal R, I.radical = maximalIdeal R ∧ I.spanFinrank = n} d] := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_nat_ringKrullDim R
  have hHS : Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = (e : WithBot ℕ) :=
    hilbertSamuelDegree_eq_ringKrullDim R he
  have h1 : (ringKrullDim R = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) ↔ d = e := by
    rw [he]
    exact ⟨fun h => by exact_mod_cast h.symm, fun h => by rw [h]⟩
  have h2 : (Module.hilbertSamuelDegree R R = (d : WithBot ℕ)) ↔ d = e := by
    rw [hHS]
    exact ⟨fun h => by exact_mod_cast h.symm, fun h => by rw [h]⟩
  have h3 :
    IsLeast {n : ℕ | ∃ I : Ideal R, I.radical = maximalIdeal R ∧ I.spanFinrank = n} d ↔ d = e :=
    ⟨fun h => h.unique (isLeast_spanFinrank he), fun h => h ▸ isLeast_spanFinrank he⟩
  tfae_have 1 ↔ 2 := by rw [h1, item_two_iff, h2]
  tfae_have 1 ↔ 3 := by rw [h1, h3]
  tfae_finish

end Computes

end Stacks.HilbertSamuel.DimensionTheorem

/-- **Dimension of a Noetherian local ring.** For a Noetherian local ring `(R, m)` and a natural
number `d` the following are equivalent: `dim(R) = d`; the Hilbert–Samuel function
`n ↦ length_R (R / m ^ (n + 1))` is eventually a `ℤ`-combination
`∑_{i ≤ d} (n choose i) * a i` of binomial coefficients with `a d ≠ 0`, i.e. `d(R) = d`; and `d`
is the least number of generators of an ideal of definition of `R`, i.e. some ideal of definition
is generated by `d` elements and none is generated by fewer. -/
@[stacks 00KQ "Items (1)-(3); see the module docstring for the form of (2) and (3).", ega "0 16.2.5"
  "local case", ega "IV 5.1.6"]
public theorem IsLocalRing.ringKrullDim_eq_tfae {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] (d : ℕ) :
    List.TFAE
      [ringKrullDim R = d,
        ∃ a : ℕ → ℤ,
          a d ≠ 0 ∧
            ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop,
              ∃ p : ℕ,
                Module.length R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) = p ∧
                  (p : ℤ) = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (d + 1), (n.choose i : ℤ) * a i,
        IsLeast {n : ℕ | ∃ I : Ideal R, I.radical = maximalIdeal R ∧ I.spanFinrank = n} d] :=
  Stacks.HilbertSamuel.DimensionTheorem.solution d

end
